"கன்று","lemma":"கன்று","gloss":"calves"},{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":"many"}],"gloss":"many calves"},{"surface":"கெழீஇய","parts":[{"text":"கெழீஇய","lemma":"கெழீஇய","gloss":"abounding"}],"gloss":"abounding","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கான்கெழு","parts":[{"text":"கான்","lemma":"கான்","gloss":"forest"},{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"கெழு","gloss":"abounding"}],"gloss":"forest-abounding"},{"surface":"நாடன்","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"நாடு","gloss":"land"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"he of"}],"gloss":"lord of the land"},{"surface":"நெடுந்தேர்","parts":[{"text":"நெடுந்தேர்","lemma":"நெடுந்தேர்","gloss":"tall chariot"}],"gloss":"tall chariot","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அவியன்","parts":[{"text":"அவியன்","lemma":"அவியன்","gloss":"Aviyan"}],"gloss":"Aviyan"},{"surface":"என","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":"called"}],"gloss":"called"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஒருவனை","parts":[{"text":"ஒருவன்","lemma":"ஒருவன்","gloss":"one man"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ஐ","gloss":"accusative"}],"gloss":"one man"},{"surface":"உடையேன்","parts":[{"text":"உடை","lemma":"உடை","gloss":"possess"},{"text":"ஏன்","lemma":"ஏன்","gloss":"I"}],"gloss":"I have"},{"surface":"மன்னே","parts":[{"text":"மன்","lemma":"மன்","gloss":"indeed"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"யானே","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"யான்","gloss":"I"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"I"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அறான்","parts":[{"text":"அறான்","lemma":"அறான்","gloss":"generous one"}],"gloss":"generous one"},{"surface":"எவன்","parts":[{"text":"எவன்","lemma":"எவன்","gloss":"how"}],"gloss":"how"},{"surface":"பரிகோ","parts":[{"text":"பரி","lemma":"பரி","gloss":"lament"},{"text":"கோ","lemma":"கோ","gloss":"I"}],"gloss":"shall I lament"},{"surface":"வெள்ளியது","parts":[{"text":"வெள்ளி","lemma":"வெள்ளி","gloss":"Venus"},{"text":"அது","lemma":"அது","gloss":"its"}],"gloss":"of Venus"},{"surface":"நிலையே","parts":[{"text":"நிலை","lemma":"நிலை","gloss":"position"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"position"}]}],"literal":"Bright-spotted rooster waking me up, rising up quickly / cool dew dripping, undawned early morning / fine stick small drum resounding, striking / tall gate standing, many oxen praising / his fame I praised as, shunning meat / well-guarded vast mansion approaching, desiring / opening bud soft bond unfolded water lily / honey-flowing having inside their fragrant petals having / snake sloughed skin like having the form of bamboo / born of bamboo peel like thread beauty invisible / bright flowered fine cloth having worn, fine ornaments / slender and curved waist of, beautifully curved navel / chaste wife her side to embrace / me who turned looking at … / … with stones / having destroyed that which was born I having become, in that way / others greatness fame singing, affliction I do not know / for the small udder yearning milk drinking white kid / grey-faced langur with leaping … / … many calves abounding / forest-abounding lord of the land tall chariot Aviyan called / one man I have indeed I / generous one how shall I lament of Venus position","translation":"Woken by the bright-spotted rooster, I rose early in the cool, dew-dripping dawn. Striking my small drum with a fine stick, I stood at the tall gate, praising his great oxen and singing his fame. Desiring to enter his well-guarded, vast mansion, I shunned ordinary meat. There, his chaste wife, wearing a fine cloth as thin as a snake's sloughed skin or the peel of a bamboo, adorned with fine ornaments on her slender waist and curved navel, embraced him. Looking at me who turned... with stones... having destroyed my poverty, I became prosperous. Since then, I have never known the affliction of singing the praises of others. I have Aviyan, the lord of the forest-abounding land where white kids yearn for the small udder and grey-faced langurs leap, as my sole protector. Why then should I worry about the position of Venus?","modern":"ஒளிரும் புள்ளிகளையுடைய சேவல் எழுப்ப, குளிர்ந்த பனி சொட்டும் விடியற்காலையில் நான் எழுந்தேன். மெல்லிய குச்சியால் சிறு கிணையை முழக்கி, அவனது பெரிய வாயிலில் நின்று, அவனது எருதுகளை வாழ்த்தி அவனது புகழைப் பாடினேன். அவனது காவல் மிகுந்த பெரிய மாளிகையை அடைய விரும்பி, புலால் உணவை வெறுத்தேன். பாம்பின் சட்டை போன்றதும் மூங்கிலின் உரிக்கப்பட்ட தோல் போன்றதுமான மெல்லிய ஆடையை உடுத்தி, நுண்ணிய அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த அவனது கற்புடைய மனைவி அவனைத் தழுவினாள். என்னை நோக்கி... கற்களைக் கொண்டு... வறுமையை அழித்து நான் புதுப்பிறவி எடுத்தேன். அதன் பிறகு பிறருடைய புகழைப் பாடித் திரியும் துன்பத்தை நான் அறியேன். முலைப்பாலுக்காகத் தவிக்கும் வெள்ளாட்டுக்குட்டிகள் சாம்பல் நிற முகமுடைய குரங்குகளோடு விளையாடும் காடுகள் நிறைந்த நாட்டின் தலைவனும், நெடுந்தேரை உடையவனுமாகிய அவியன் என்னும் ஒருவனை மட்டுமே நான் தலைவனாகப் பெற்றுள்ளேன். இனி நான் வெள்ளிக்கோளின் நிலையைப் பற்றி ஏன் கவலைப்பட வேண்டும்?","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai and depicts the theme of Kaṭainilai (waiting at the gate of a patron). The poet, Māṟōkkattu Nappacalaiyār, praises a generous patron named Aviyaṉ. The poet describes waking up early in the morning, beating the small drum, and standing at the patron's gate to sing his praises. The description of the patron's wife wearing extremely fine, translucent garments (compared to a snake's sloughed skin or bamboo peel) highlights the wealth and aesthetic refinement of the household. Having received the patron's immense generosity, which completely destroyed his poverty, the poet declares that he no longer needs to beg or sing the praises of other lords. The poem ends with a confident assertion that as long as he has Aviyaṉ as his protector, he does not need to worry about astrological portents like the position of Venus, which traditionally indicates rain or drought.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.47],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.4],[1.4,2.0],[2.0,3.0],[3.0,3.1],[3.1,3.6],[3.6,3.8],[3.8,5.0],[5.0,5.5],[5.5,5.72],[5.8,6.02],[6.1,7.2],[7.2,7.2],[7.2,8.0